{"id": "EUVD-2026-97873", "enisaUuid": "f32261b0-6fd0-30a0-b8b1-aece22707365", "description": "Vercel deepsec from 0.1.0 before 1.1.17 contains a link following vulnerability in extractTarballLocally that allows sandboxed code to write files outside the sandbox by planting links in result tarballs. Attackers controlling sandbox code, such as a prompt-injected coding agent, can plant symbolic or hard links in the host data directory to write arbitrary files on the orchestrator host.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T20:55:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:45:01", "baseScore": 4.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:H/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vercel-labs/deepsec/pull/46", "https://github.com/vercel-labs/deepsec/pull/47", "https://github.com/vercel-labs/deepsec/commit/c5a4e4220ece72aee67c2ea21f4340e65f673fc1", "https://github.com/vercel-labs/deepsec", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vercel-deepsec-before-1.1.17-arbitrary-file-write-via-symlink-in-sandbox-tarball-extraction"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109375", "GHSA-cchp-25pr-r776"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4e31d2b6-ccfa-3fdd-9544-6b2a04a0466b", "product": {"name": "deepsec", "vendor": {"name": "vercel"}}, "product_version": "0.1.0 <1.1.17"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "318d3594-f97f-3df7-b26b-9bdb38928abd", "vendor": {"name": "vercel"}}], "isExploited": false}